(Distributed Systems - Study Notes) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. CAP Theorem) Tj
T*
(A distributed data store can only guarantee two of the following three:) Tj
T*
(Consistency, Availability and Partition tolerance. Because network) Tj
T*
(partitions are unavoidable in a real cluster, the practical choice is) Tj
T*
(between consistency and availability during a partition.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(CP systems reject writes when a partition prevents quorum, which keeps) Tj
T*
(every reader on the same value. AP systems keep serving reads and writes) Tj
T*
(and reconcile conflicts later, usually with last-write-wins or CRDTs.) Tj
