(2. Consistency Models) Tj
T*
(Linearizability gives the illusion of a single copy updated atomically.) Tj
T*
(Sequential consistency preserves each client's program order but allows) Tj
T*
(reordering across clients. Causal consistency only orders operations that) Tj
T*
(are causally related, which is enough for many collaborative editors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Replication) Tj
T*
(Single-leader replication is simple to reason about but the leader is a) Tj
T*
(bottleneck and a failover risk. Multi-leader replication tolerates) Tj
T*
(regional outages at the cost of write conflicts. Leaderless replication) Tj
T*
(uses quorums: with R + W > N, every read overlaps the latest write.) Tj
ET
endstream
